#X obj 675 11 list.each;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 215 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 the object passes each element (or a group of @step
elements) of the input list through the rightmost outlet to an external
object \, which is expected to return the processed value back to the
rightmost inlet;
#X text 240 153 this allows arbitrary mapping \, transformation and
filtering of list values via a side-chain \, for example applying a
function to every element or grouping elements before processing;
#X text 240 223 the object can be used to apply the same operation
to every list element \, for example to square all values or to multiply
every third element;
